# .bobignore — DEFENSE-IN-DEPTH only. NOT the isolation wall.
# It is one workspace-global file: it applies to every mode the same way, so it
# cannot express "witness is walled from src/ but surgeon is not".
# The real wall is declarative Bob configuration in .bob/custom_modes.yaml:
# per-mode tool groups + a fileRegex on each mode's `edit` group, backed by the
# mode-scoped rules in .bob/rules-<slug>/. See the header of custom_modes.yaml.
#
# So this file only lists paths that NO mode should ever read or write.

# Build artifacts / deps
node_modules/
dist/
build/

# Sensitive config
.env
.env.*

# Secrets / local state fixtures we don't want read broadly
fixtures/secrets/
*.key
*.pem

# Large / temp
*.tmp
*.log
.cache/

# NOTE: we deliberately do NOT ignore src/ here, because surgeon and
# control-agent MUST read it. Keeping witness/isolate off src/ is the job of
# their mode definitions (no edit access to src/, no shell) and their
# .bob/rules-<slug>/ instructions — not this file.
# NOTE: .bob/scratch/ is NOT ignored: mutineer writes its mutation report there
# and isolate must read it.
